  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India - Production of textiles</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Khaloom focuses on producing handwoven fabrics with a own weaving mill where (partly) recycled materials are used.At the end of 2019, it set up its own production location with a DGGF Starter Loan where mainly women perform work at a fair wage.Part of the company is also the extensive training and education of employees and transfer of knowledge (both operational and managerial).For a further roll-out of Khaloom&apos;s business model, it is necessary to invest in commerce, expansion of production and development of the organization. With these 3 elements, Khaloom can shape her strategy and faster andcreate more impact through introduce the sustainable and fair way of working andproduction to other textile producers.</narrative>
  </description>
